target/
_apalache-out/
remotion/node_modules/
remotion/out/

# Generated by the demos and by the Bitcoin backend. These are *outputs*, not
# fixtures: `./demo/local2.sh` rebuilds its directory from nothing every run.
# uv-demo2/ was missed when local2.sh replaced the old demo, and the result was
# 3.6M lines of committed proof bytes — 99.6% of the repository, rewritten on
# every amend.
uv-poc-data/
uv-demo2/
uv-record-index.json

# The iOS static library is a build output: `ios/README.md` documents copying it
# in from target/ before the Xcode build. 21 MB of compiled Rust does not belong
# in the tree.
ios/libuv_iosffi.a
# Same for the wallet app: `ios/build-wallet.sh` puts the per-platform static
# library here, and generates the .xcodeproj from `project.yml`. A pbxproj is a
# merge hazard and an opaque diff; the generator spec is the reviewable thing.
ios/UVWallet/lib/
ios/UVWallet/UVWallet.xcodeproj/

# Output of demo/relay.sh: two wallet homes and the relay bag.
uv-relay-demo/
uv-relay-data/

# `air/mutants.py`'s backups of the constraint sources while it swaps mutated
# copies in. Ignored because the *other* half of this failure already bit: a
# run killed by SIGTERM left a mutated `wots_air.rs` in the tree, and these
# files are its siblings. A committed `.orig` is only clutter, but it is
# clutter that looks exactly like the thing that is not (see air/COVERAGE.md).
air/src/*.rs.orig

# Not this project's. `@openai/codex-security` and its 399 MB of vendored
# binaries appeared in the repo root from another tool on the machine, and a
# `git add -A` swept them into the commit — GitHub rejected the push over a
# 248 MB file, which is the only reason anyone noticed. The files are left on
# disk; they are simply not ours to commit.
node_modules/
package.json
package-lock.json

# Python bytecode (the mutation harness is a script, not a package)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
